  "body": "Three bespoke waterfront architectural homes, designed by Cheshire Architects and brought to life through a stunning collaboration of industry-leading craftspeople. These exquisite new three-bedroom homes on the shores of Kohimarama Beach are a sensory homecoming to the urban beachside lifestyle you’ve been longing for.\r\n\r\nGracing the inner Auckland coastline, the elegant brick façade of this brand new architectural masterpiece stands anchored aside the ocean at 293 Tamaki Drive, offering uninterrupted vistas across the Waitemata to Rangitoto.\r\n\r\nEach home features spacious interior living, curated to provide a sense of ease and a connection to the surrounding environment, with carefully proportioned glazing, and a curated palette of organic, textural materials that echo nature’s tones, providing an elegance that will only improve with time.\r\n\r\nExquisite Molteni & C kitchens form the centre of the homes, flowing seamlessly to the open plan living spaces, and for 2 homes, onto a spacious wintergarden terrace that opens each home to the coastal setting while allowing for sheltered enjoyment. Complementing the curated materiality through the homes, the built form creates an immersive interplay of light, texture and shadow, all framed by expansive ocean views beyond.\r\n\r\nNo detail has been spared in materiality or execution, with design decisions at every stage elevating Beachhouse’s finish to the highest level for a living experience that leaves nothing to be desired.\r\n\r\nThe sleek architectural façade is finished with custom 400mm slimline Canterbury Clay bricks, installed by highly skilled master bricklayers, and features thermally broken, double glazed aluminium window joinery to offer superior thermal and acoustic performance. Sliding doors feature custom solid bronze handles, and the frameless stacking glass doors fully enclose the heated wintergarden loggias enabling year-round comfort and enjoyment. Beautiful custom steel window joinery is a feature to each entrance lobby. Solid concrete walls and floors have a buildup of almost 0.5m, while windows feature deep window reveals; all designed to an acoustic rating of STC 65 which means each home is ensconced in silence and privacy. Venting and downpipes have been carefully built in, maintaining excellent ventilation properties without compromising the seamless exterior aesthetic.\r\n\r\nInside, custom Forte oak flooring, hand plastered wall finishes in living and master suite, Egyptian limestone walls and floors in the bathrooms,100% wool hand-loomed Artisan carpets, with bronze detailing elements throughout the homes and ECC lighting providing exquisite finishing touches. Oak features extensively, in the custom Cheshire-designed vanities and joinery, as well as the Molteni & C kitchens, and wardrobes which are finished with linen front doors. High end appliances from Sub Zero and Gaggenau, Astra Walker English Brass finished tapware, careful consideration of water and ducting services, and integrated electronic automated security and access control all ensure an unparalleled luxury home experience.\r\n\r\nSituated in enviable waterfront position along Kohimarama’s promenade, residents are at the heart of the exclusive inner East beach suburbs. Kohimarama Beach is all yours, right on the doorstep for sunrise strolls and a coffee at the Kohi Beach Eatery & Store just two blocks distant. Neighbouring St Heliers and Mission Bay lie mere minutes away either side, and the entertainments of Auckland City Centre are closer than you think, just a short drive along the water.\r\n\r\nThere are many thoughtful details and non-code-compulsory upgrades that make these homes so special inside and out. Beachhouse presents a rare find where the team’s dedication to quality is seen and felt at every level, ensuring long-term performance and peace of mind for the inhabitants who will own this piece of beachfront luxury. You truly need to see the detailing for yourself to know. Organise a private tour and let us show you through in person. Call Aaron to arrange your tour.",
